.PP
.SS "Basic Usage"
.SS "Changing animation delay"
Use the \fRdelay-{amount}\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-delay\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce delay\-150 duration\-300 \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce delay\-300 duration\-300 \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce delay\-700 duration\-300 \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation delay\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing animation direction"
Use the \fRdirection-{keyword}\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-delay\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce direction\-normal \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce direction\-reverse \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce direction\-alternate \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce direction\-alternate\-reverse \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation direction\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing animation duration"
Use the \fRduration-{amount}\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-duration\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce duration\-150 \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce duration\-300 \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce duration\-700 \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation duration\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing animation fill mode"
Use the \fRfill-mode-{keyword}\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-fill-mode\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce fill\-mode\-none \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce fill\-mode\-forwards \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce fill\-mode\-backwards \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce fill\-mode\-both \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation fill mode\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing animation iteration count"
Use the \fRrepeat-{amount}\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-iteration-count\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce repeat\-0 \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce repeat\-1 \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce repeat\-infinite \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation iteration count\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing animation play state"
Use the \fRrunning\fP and \fRpaused\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-play-state\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce running \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce paused \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation play state\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing animation timing function"
Use the \fRease-{keyword}\fP utilities to control an element’s \fRanimation-timing-function\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-bounce ease\-linear \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce ease\-in \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce ease\-out \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
<button class="animate\-bounce ease\-in\-out \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBanimation timing function\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Prefers-reduced-motion"
For situations where the user has specified that they prefer reduced motion, you can conditionally apply animations and transitions using the \fRmotion-safe\fP and \fRmotion-reduce\fP variants:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="motion\-safe:animate\-bounce \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
.fi
.PP
.SS "Enter & Exit Animations"
.SS "Adding enter animations"
To give an element an enter animation, use the \fRanimate-in\fP utility, in combination with some \fB\fRfade-in\fP\fP, \fB\fRspin-in\fP\fP, \fB\fRzoom-in\fP\fP, and \fB\fRslide-in-from\fP\fP utilities\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-in fade\-in \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-in spin\-in \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-in zoom\-in \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
<button class="animate\-in slide\-in\-from\-top \&.\&.\&.">Button D</button>
<button class="animate\-in slide\-in\-from\-left \&.\&.\&.">Button E</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBenter animation\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Adding exit animations"
To give an element an exit animation, use the \fRanimate-out\fP utility, in combination with some \fB\fRfade-out\fP\fP, \fB\fRspin-out\fP\fP, \fB\fRzoom-out\fP\fP, and \fB\fRslide-out-from\fP\fP utilities\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<button class="animate\-out fade\-out \&.\&.\&.">Button A</button>
<button class="animate\-out spin\-out \&.\&.\&.">Button B</button>
<button class="animate\-out zoom\-out \&.\&.\&.">Button C</button>
<button class="animate\-out slide\-out\-from\-top \&.\&.\&.">Button D</button>
<button class="animate\-out slide\-out\-from\-left \&.\&.\&.">Button E</button>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Learn more in the \fBexit animation\fP documentation\&.
.SS "Changing enter animation starting opacity"
Set the starting opacity of an animation using the \fRfade-in-{amount}\fP utilities\&.

.PP
.PP
